        "body": {
            "type": "TextualBody",
            "frametrail:type": "text",
            "format": "text/html",
            "value": "",
            "frametrail:name": "Where the launcher came from",
            "frametrail:attributes": {
                "text": "&lt;div class=&quot;dossierNote&quot; data-layer=&quot;3&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;dossierLayer&quot;&gt;Open sources&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;dossierTitle&quot;&gt;Where the launcher came from&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Damage to the rubber side skirt works like a fingerprint. It matches a launcher filmed in late June in a convoy from Kursk to Millerovo, of Russia&amp;#x27;s 53rd Anti-Aircraft Missile Brigade. The findings were given to the investigation team.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;dossierLink&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.bellingcat.com/news/uk-and-europe/2015/10/08/mh17-the-open-source-evidence/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener&quot;&gt;Bellingcat: MH17 – The Open Source Evidence ↗&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;"
            }
        }
